From: ROCKNIX <rocknix@rocknix.org>
Date: Sun, 05 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: add XDP mark-triggered PPE soft hook for selective offload

Add a soft hook in the RX NAPI path that triggers immediate PPE flow
promotion when skb->mark indicates an XDP-classified bulk or normal
traffic flow (marks 0xAF01 and 0xAF02). This bypasses the hardware
rate threshold (PPE_CPU_REASON_HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED) for flows
already classified by the XDP program.

The mark is set by the XDP classifier via metadata at data-64 (magic
0xA1B2C3D4). Interactive (0xAF03) and realtime (0xAF04) flows are
excluded to preserve CPU-side AQM for latency-sensitive traffic.

The pr_debug line is compiled out unless dynamic debug is enabled,
adding zero overhead in production.

Signed-off-by: ROCKNIX <rocknix@rocknix.org>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -962,9 +962,14 @@ static int airoha_qdma_rx_process(struct
 				     PKT_HASH_TYPE_L4);
 
 		reason = FIELD_GET(AIROHA_RXD4_PPE_CPU_REASON, msg1);
-		if (reason == PPE_CPU_REASON_HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED)
-			airoha_ppe_check_skb(&eth->ppe->dev, q->skb, hash,
-					     false);
+		if (reason == PPE_CPU_REASON_HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED ||
+		    (q->skb->mark >= 0xAF01 && q->skb->mark <= 0xAF02 &&
+		     hash != AIROHA_RXD4_FOE_ENTRY)) {
+			pr_debug("airoha_soft_hook: hash=%u mark=0x%x reason=%u\n",
+				 hash, q->skb->mark, reason);
+			airoha_ppe_check_skb(&eth->ppe->dev, q->skb, hash,
+					     false);
+		}
 
 		done++;
 		napi_gro_receive(&q->napi, q->skb);
